  "$comment": "The buyer signs a GET to https://seller.example.com/proposals?f=a|b, and the request carries that URL as a caller writes it. Its @target-uri is https://seller.example.com/proposals?f=a|b: the URL as an HTTP client sends it and a server receives it, the WHATWG URL serialization normalized per RFC 3986 section 6.2.2 (lowercase scheme and host, no default port, no dot segments), with every character a client sends raw left as written. A verifier that parses the URL with a stricter grammar, re-encodes it, or skips the normalization computes another signature base and refuses a valid request."
